{"uid":"87cb69297b5d2728","name":"TestKubeRegistrationSuite/TestKubeRegistrationLonghornDisks","fullName":"github.com/lf-edge/eve/evetest/tests/kuberegistration.TestKubeRegistrationSuite/TestKubeRegistrationLonghornDisks","time":{"start":1795645353000,"stop":1795645354500,"duration":1500},"status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[],"testStage":{"steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"hasContent":false,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"attachmentStep":false},"afterStages":[],"labels":[{"name":"resultFormat","value":"junit"},{"name":"suite","value":"github.com/lf-edge/eve/evetest/tests/kuberegistration"},{"name":"testClass","value":"github.com/lf-edge/eve/evetest/tests/kuberegistration"},{"name":"package","value":"github.com/lf-edge/eve/evetest/tests/kuberegistration"}],"parameters":[],"links":[],"hidden":false,"retry":false,"extra":{"severity":"normal","retries":[],"categories":[],"history":{"statistic":{"failed":2,"broken":0,"skipped":0,"passed":26,"unknown":0,"total":28},"items":[{"uid":"9383d6874a9b1df1","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/51/#testresult/9383d6874a9b1df1","status":"passed","time":{"start":1795565028000,"stop":1795565029470,"duration":1470}},{"uid":"d3e851d190714b7a","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/46/#testresult/d3e851d190714b7a","status":"passed","time":{"start":1795505342000,"stop":1795505343570,"duration":1570}},{"uid":"515b659b11e09be7","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/41/#testresult/515b659b11e09be7","status":"failed","statusDetails":"No cluster was set up: TestKubeRegistrationSuite/TestKubeRegistrationLonghornDisks builds on the cluster that TestKubeRegistrationClusterSetup forms, so it only runs as part of TestKubeRegistrationSuite\n\nClaude's conclusion:\nThis confirms the cascade: this test's own \"Setup complete\" happened fine (devices onboarded and booting — matching the live status I see now), but it immediately failed via `requireKubeRegCluster` → \"No cluster was set up,\" the same guard-clause panic as `TestKubeRegistrationAddNode`.\n\n### Root cause\n\nThis is not an independent failure — it's a third cascading symptom of the same root cause already documented in `live-investigation.md` for this run. `TestKubeRegistrationClusterSetup` failed at 22:48:55 because the Proxmox broker returned `500 user name not set` while provisioning VM 113 for `edge-dev2` — a broker-side auth/session error, not an EVE/pillar bug. Every subsequent sub-test in `TestKubeRegistrationSuite` (`TestKubeRegistrationAddNode`, and now `TestKubeRegistrationLonghornDisks`) builds its own fresh devices successfully (as seen live: all 4 devices are currently up and in `BOOTING` state, onboarded fine) but then immediately fails in `requireKubeRegCluster` (`helpers_test.go:151`) because no kube cluster was ever actually formed in this run — that guard only checks a run-level flag set by `ClusterSetup`, independent of whether new devices boot correctly.\n\nPer `live-ledger.md`, the underlying `\"500 user name not set\"` broker error is a known, recurring (if infrequent) flake first seen on 2026-11-09 (run #12, `TestNodeClusterSuite/TestMgmtProxy`), part of a broader class of Proxmox-broker VM-provisioning instability. No PR diff was supplied, so no RELATED verdict is given.","time":{"start":1795387657000,"stop":1795387921400,"duration":264400}},{"uid":"c7c1062d59f83eb4","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/36/#testresult/c7c1062d59f83eb4","status":"passed","time":{"start":1795307461000,"stop":1795307462440,"duration":1440}},{"uid":"94d923768dadd7c1","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/31/#testresult/94d923768dadd7c1","status":"passed","time":{"start":1795213040000,"stop":1795213041590,"duration":1590}},{"uid":"74b3d5a2ab7817e5","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.